cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If QUARTIC2D contributes to published research, cite the archived software release used in the calculation."
title: "QUARTIC2D: Quadrature for Radial Tetra-center Interaction Coefficients in 2D"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  QUARTIC2D evaluates four-center interaction matrix elements for generalized
  localized orbital bases in two dimensions with translationally invariant
  radial kernels. The method represents real or complex transition fields in
  angular harmonics and reduces the interaction to radial Hankel integrals.
  It supports direct, exchange, pair-hopping, correlated-hopping, and related
  four-index couplings used to parameterize Hubbard-like and multiorbital
  effective Hamiltonians within the radial-kernel assumption.
authors:
  - family-names: "Santacruz"
    given-names: "Alex"
keywords:
  - four-center interactions
  - interaction matrix elements
  - Hankel transform
  - angular harmonics
  - two-dimensional materials
  - quantum materials
  - Wannier functions
repository-code: "https://github.com/QuantumArtificer/quartic2d"
url: "https://quantumartificer.github.io/quartic2d/"
license: MIT
